  <section id="best-for">
    <h2>Who Caribbean Beach is best for</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Anyone who wants the Skyliner at a Moderate rate.</strong> The station is on the resort, and the lines go to EPCOT, Hollywood Studios, and the Pop Century / Art of Animation station.</li>
      <li><strong>Families who want two queen beds</strong> and, in some rooms, a child-size pull-down bed, without paying Deluxe prices. In 2026 a Standard Location room ran about $310 to $523 a night at full price, tax included.</li>
      <li><strong>People who want a sit-down restaurant on site.</strong> Sebastian's Bistro is table service, and there are two quick-service spots plus a pool bar.</li>
    </ul>
    <h3>Think twice if…</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>You don't want to walk.</strong> This is a spread-out resort. Preferred rooms are listed as closer to Centertown, dining, shopping or transportation. Standard rooms can be a longer walk to the Skyliner and the food.</li>
      <li><strong>Your parks are mostly Magic Kingdom or Animal Kingdom.</strong> Those are buses. The Skyliner is the advantage here.</li>
      <li><strong>Your trip falls on Jan 24–30, 2027, or Jan 24–Feb 2, 2028.</strong> Official pages say the Skyliner is closed for routine refurbishment then, with buses filling in.</li>
    </ul>
    <span class="ryan">[Ryan: who you think this resort is really for, from your own stays. Two or three sentences.]</span>
  </section>

