  <section id="booking">
    <h2>Booking and value tips</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Book a Standard Location room if you don't mind walking.</strong> In 2026 those rooms ran about $310 to $523 a night at full price including tax, depending on dates. Preferred Location rooms ran about $396 to $627. King rooms ran about $374 to $590.</li>
      <li><strong>Pay for Preferred if the shorter walk to Centertown or the Skyliner matters.</strong> The room is the same layout.</li>
      <li><strong>If you need a fifth bed for a child, confirm a room with the pull-down bed</strong> when you book. Not every standard room includes it.</li>
      <li><strong>Extra adults cost more.</strong> Moderate rates assume two adults. Each extra adult adds $25 a night plus tax, and kids under 18 are free.</li>
      <li><strong>Check Disney's own offers page first.</strong> Disney points to <a href="https://disneyworld.disney.go.com/special-offers/">its special offers page</a> for discounts. Our deals hub will track current ones.</li>
      <li><strong>Avoid Jan 24–30, 2027, and Jan 24–Feb 2, 2028</strong> if the Skyliner is why you are booking this resort.</li>
      <li><strong>Lightning Lane head start:</strong> Disney resort guests can buy Lightning Lane passes up to 7 days before their stay.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="fg-callout">
      <h3>Rates change</h3>
